Goal:
To extract the password for this level by submitting current level's password to
port 30001 on localhost using SSL/TLS encryption.

Connect:
use the script in the useful scripts to autofill

Approach:
I started by googling what is the command that is used to send request using the
SSL/TLS encryption. which led me to openssl which was also mentioned in the 
useful commands.

I tried a brute force way to 'man openssl | grep CONNECTED COMMANDS' this yeilded 
ntg significant.

Then i tried to brute force the openssl command whose error message prompted me to
search and specify a command that is used to encrypt the connection. 

Command:
openssl s_client -connect localhost:30001

Breakdown:
The general syntax for openssl is:

openssl cmd [option] destination 

Result:
After succesful connection we are prompted to enter the password of the current level
which revealed the answer for the next level. 

Key Takeaway:
This was a really mindbreaking room for me to figure out whichcommand to use 
with the correct corresponding option.
This room gave a very hands-on approach to the modern day SSL/TLS HTTPS protocol 
that was only theoretical knowledge to me before.

